  "result": "Perfect! The tier discount feature is complete and working correctly. Here's a summary:\n\n## Customer Tier Discounts \u2014 Implementation Complete \u2705\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**1. Tier Discount Configuration** (`src/customers.js`)\n- Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant centralized in one place:\n  - `gold`: 5%\n  - `silver`: 2.5%\n  - `standard`: 0%\n\n**2. createInvoice Enhancement** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- Retrieves customer tier and applies discount to lines that don't have an explicit `discountPercent`\n- Logic: explicit discountPercent (even 0) always wins over tier discount\n- Lines without explicit discountPercent automatically get the customer's tier discount\n\n**3. addLine Enhancement** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- Applies tier discount when adding a new line without explicit discountPercent\n- Does NOT change discount when just increasing qty on existing line\n- Allows overriding tier discount with explicit discountPercent\n\n### Behavior:\n\n| Scenario | Result |\n|----------|--------|\n| Gold customer, no explicit discount | Gets 5% tier discount |\n| Silver customer, no explicit discount | Gets 2.5% tier discount |\n| Standard customer, no explicit discount | Gets 0% tier discount |\n| Any tier + explicit discountPercent | Uses explicit value |\n| Gold customer + explicit 0% | No discount (explicit wins) |\n\n### Tests Added (9 new tests):\n\n- Tier discount application for gold/silver/standard\n- Explicit discount overriding tier discount\n- 0% override over tier discount\n- Mixed discount and tier-discount lines\n- addLine tier discount behavior\n- Updating existing line preserves discount\n\n**Total: 96 tests pass** (87 existing + 9 new tier tests)",
